"Hard to tell," I say, leaning back against the cold stone. "Depends on whether it keeps its word. At the very least, it wants the king dead just as badly as we do."

"To the abyss with the machine!" Hadrik says. "It's iron and wire. The rebels have the steel. Can we trust them to mount a raid?"

"The rebels won't touch the towers," Kate says, her arms folded tightly across her cloak. "Their king made that clear. He won't spend a single soldier on a rescue, even knowing innocent people are strapped to the drain. The only thing an alliance gets us is steel against the palace on the surface. Nothing more."

