ID: B3-Ch05a-Mock
TEXT:

#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 0) {
"What's wrong, Albert?" I call out. "Relegated to hallway guard? The underground's deadliest blade, playing nursemaid to refugees?"

Albert glares daggers at me, saying nothing, his hand twitching near his hilt as he brushes past without slowing down.

Hadrik chuckles, his axe shifting on his shoulder. "You two really don't see eye to eye, do you?"

"Occupational hazard," I say. "Never had much luck with assassins."

The moment the heavy timber door thuds shut behind us, Daren sets his shield down and tends to Illuna. For all her iron composure, the dark cloth of her tunic is soaked through with blood from where the lessathi assassin's dagger punched into her flank. Daren kneels in his scuffed plate, his gauntlets off, hands bathing the wound in a soft, steady white glow. Muscle and skin knit back together under the light while Illuna keeps her breathing measured and her eyes blank.

